What is a Sealed Class?
A Sealed Class restricts which classes can extend or implement it.


Why Do We Need Sealed Classes?
✅ Restrict inheritance
✅ Improve security
✅ Better domain modeling
✅ More predictable code
✅ Useful with Pattern Matching and Switch expressions

allows developers to control which classes can extend or implement a class or interface using the permits keyword. It provides restricted inheritance, improving security and maintainability. Unlike a final class, which prevents all inheritance, a sealed class allows inheritance only to a predefined set of subclasses. This is particularly useful for domain models like Payment, Vehicle, and Shape hierarchies.
